I've recently started an attempt to convert Nethack to T-Engine 3, an
opensource roguelike engine where everything is described in LUA, and
I've run into a small problem during the monster conversion; that is,
none of the monster spoilers I've looked at [mon1-343.txt &
mon2-343.txt, in particular] list how big the hit dice are. They do
specify how *many* HD monsters have, but they only specify a formula to
determine hit points if the HD is >50.

The source isn't particularly clear on this point either, unless there
is a comment I missed when I looked at monst.c.

For reference, the idea behind the conversion is that it's easier to
add/modify bits in the engine when knowledge of C isn't required. [The
working title of the project is ODEHack, as I'm using the ODE module
for T-Engine 3 as a base, since it's mostly a half-baked Rogue clone.]

You can find T-Engine 3 at http://www.t-o-m-e.net .



